# Environment Configuration

This file contains environment variables required for authentication with Supabase.

Copy this template to `.env.local` and replace the placeholder values with your actual Supabase project credentials:

```env
# Supabase Configuration
# Get your project credentials from Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key-here

# Application URL — used for OAuth redirect URLs
# Local dev: http://localhost:3000
# Production (Vercel): https://artsfashion.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

## Environment Variables

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`: The URL of your Supabase project
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`: The publishable (public) API key for your Supabase project
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`: The application URL for OAuth redirects. Set to `http://localhost:3000` for local development, and to your production domain (e.g. `https://artsfashion.vercel.app`) in your deployment platform's environment variables

## Setup Steps

1. Create a Supabase project at [supabase.com](https://supabase.com)
2. Navigate to Project Settings -> API in the Supabase Dashboard
3. Copy the values for `URL` and `publishable key`
4. Paste them into your `.env.local` file
5. Restart your development server

## Security Notes

- Never commit your `.env.local` file to version control
- Add `.env.local` to your `.gitignore` file
- These credentials provide public access to your Supabase project
